  "executive_narrative": "### Executive Performance Synthesis\n2017: 44,579 orders, R$ 7,142,672.43 GMV, 8.69% Net Margin, R$ 160.23 AOV | 2018: 53,775 orders, R$ 8,643,697.60 GMV, 7.97% Net Margin, R$ 160.74 AOV\n\n- **Profitability & Category Margin Recovery:** Lowest-margin volume category `construction_tools_lights` operates at 3.07% net margin (carrier cost share: 14.22%, return rate: 7.97%), while `watches_gifts` generates R$ 138,146.61 in net contribution (10.58% margin). **Action:** Re-index minimum free-freight thresholds and renegotiate carrier tier allocation on heavy/bulky SKUs where allocated carrier cost exceeds 12% of item GMV.\n- **Customer Retention & Delivery SLA Protection:** Customers exposed to late deliveries experience a sharp drop in review scores (~4.29 to ~2.57 stars) and elevated support ticket volume, directly depressing repeat purchase conversion. **Action:** Trigger automated proactive delay credits and route high-LTV cohorts away from high-late-rate interstate standard carrier lanes; deploy the 30-day post-delivery win-back voucher (EXP-01).\n- **Marketing Budget Reallocation:** Channel efficiency spans from `Organic / SEO` (ROAS nanx, CAC R$ 0.00) to `CRM / Email` (ROAS 11.50x, CAC R$ 14.46). **Action:** Shift 15-20% of spend from the lowest-ROAS paid channel into high-ROAS retention/search campaigns focused on high-repeat categories (`bed_bath_table`, `health_beauty`)."
